digraph decision {
  rankdir=TB; node [shape=box, fontname="monospace", fontsize=10];

  history [label="PRIOR-JOURNAL LESSONS APPLIED (16 folders: 11 settled with a %, 3 never filled, 2 still pending; arithmetic sum +3.69%, win rate 28.6%, avg win +1.51% / avg loss -1.12%. Small sample - no side bias inferred from it)\n1) LOSS-1.01%_2026-10-23T1024Z_ASTERUSDT (ASTER LONG 0.695 / TP 0.706 / SL 0.688): stop sat inside the rotational band, was swept, price then ran above the TP.\n   -> the long expression here would need a stop at 92.80, i.e. 0.38 inside the 92.34-93.18 sweep zone. Jev: that stop is swept first 0.60. Long rejected in that form.\n2) EXPIRED+3.95%_2026-10-18T1535Z_ASTERUSDT (ASTER LONG, TP at the range extreme): never targeted, expired +3.95%.\n   -> today the TP is 94.30, inside the 93.18-96.44 box and 1.1% above the box floor, not at the floor or the ceiling.\n3) WIN+1.26%_2026-10-27T0919Z_ASTERUSDT (ASTER SHORT 0.7150 / TP 0.7060 / SL 0.7200): entry at respected supply, stop ~0.2% above the measured regime extreme, TP inside the range - the only ASTER short that worked.\n   -> here the stop 97.20 is 0.11 above the measured 97.09 extreme of the 54h window. Flagged: it is only 0.76 above the last-31h envelope 96.44 (see conflict).\n4) EXPIRED-0.54%_2026-10-31T0901Z_XMRUSDT (SHORT 601.50 in a compression): filled, drifted, closed slightly negative at expiry.\n   -> a fade inside a compression needs a target the box actually delivers; 94.30 has been tagged four times in 40h (93.74, 93.97, 93.18, 93.83).\n5) LOSS-0.72%_2026-10-29T1149Z_BTCUSDT (SHORT 80300, post-crash supply): filled 13:15Z, stopped 14:35Z.\n   -> did not enter the post-flush tape at market; the fill requires a 1.68% retest and the stop sits outside the 30h envelope.\n6) Aggregate bias check: 8 of 11 settled trades ended by stop or negative expiry, while 3 of 4 EXPIRED-with-% trades were positive - consistent with TPs previously set beyond what the window delivers. Applied by keeping the target inside the measured box."];

  chart [label="CHART FACTS (SOLUSDT 1h, captured 2026-11-02T09:52:44Z, last bar O 94.64 H 94.90 L 94.21 C 94.51)\n13-day range: high 109.20 (2026-10-21T18:31Z) - low 92.34 (2026-10-30T00:23Z) = -15.4%.\nPath: 106.5 (20 Oct) -> 109.20 (21 Oct) -> 103.4 (22 Oct) -> 99.16 (24 Oct) -> 103.85 (28 Oct) -> 103.18 (29 Oct 17:00Z) -> flush -> 92.34 (30 Oct 00:23Z) -> 98.59 (30 Oct 05:49Z) -> 94.28 (30 Oct 18:00Z) -> 97.09 (31 Oct 01:48Z) -> 95.23 (31 Oct 08:36Z) -> 96.44 (31 Oct 12:00Z) -> 93.18 (01 Nov 22:21Z) -> 95.95 (02 Nov 03:37Z) -> 94.41 now.\nFlush detail: 2026-10-29T20:00Z bar open 99.83 -> close 96.17 (-3.7% in one hour, low 95.00).\nDescending post-flush highs: 98.59 -> 97.09 -> 96.04 (01 Nov 02:04Z) -> 95.95 (02 Nov 03:37Z).\nSupply cluster 95.90-96.44: 17 of the last 54 hourly highs printed inside it; ZERO of the last 31 hours exceeded 96.44; zero of the last 24 exceeded 95.95.\nAbove: double top 96.90 / 97.09 (31 Oct 00:00-02:00Z), untouched for 31h; 98.30-98.59 (30 Oct), untouched for 81h.\nSupport base: 93.18 (01 Nov 22:21Z) and 93.83 (02 Nov 00:22Z); hourly lows <=93.50 in the 54h window: only 4 (92.34, 93.16, 93.50 on 30 Oct; 93.18 on 01 Nov).\nVolatility: 24h range 2.98%, 30 Oct range 6.8%, 31 Oct 1.95%, 01 Nov 3.07%, 02 Nov so far 2.25%; median hourly range ~0.35%.\nVolume not visible on the chart (price-only view); taken from the exchange instead (24h 1.14M SOL)."];

  clock [label="CLOCK / LABEL RESOLUTION: chart footer reads 10:52:44 UTC+1 = 09:52:44Z, matching capture.\nTwo independent Binance pulls disagreed by exactly 1h on intraday labels (open-time vs close-time labelling).\nResolved by causality: the 20:05Z disclosure cannot drive a bar that closed at 20:00Z, so the break bar is 2026-10-29T20:00Z.\nIndependently confirmed: hourly series aggregated to daily matches the 1d candles 12/12 exactly on both H and L."];

  scen [label="SCENARIOS, 48h to 2026-11-04T10:00Z (separate Jev judgments; overlapping, NOT normalised, not a weighted distribution)\nS1 compression continues inside 93.18-96.44: P = 0.69\nS2 upside regime break (hourly close > 96.50): P = 0.25\nS3 downside break (hourly close < 93.18): P = 0.38\nS4 fresh low below the crash low 92.34: P = 0.24\nordering: P(93.30 before 96.00) = 0.45 -> P(96.00 before 93.30) ~ 0.55, up-probe first is marginally preferred\nendpoint: P(inside 94.00-96.00 at expiry) = 0.52 | P(< 93.00) = 0.18 | P(> 96.50) = 0.13 (auto 'unlikely')\ncharacter: 'descending highs mean sellers still in control' 0.71 vs 'the 29-30 Oct drop is exhaustion rather than a new leg' 0.51 -> the two halves of the read disagree, so the box is contested"];

  lev [label="LEVEL / TOUCH PROBABILITIES (48h unless stated)\ntouch 96.00: 0.68-0.70 | touch 95.90: 0.65 | touch 96.20: 0.46 | touch 97.20: 0.27\n+ sell fill 96.00 then 95.00 before 97.20: 0.65 | 94.80 before 97.20: 0.54 | 94.30 before 97.20: 0.55\n+ sell fill 95.90 then 94.30 before 97.20: 0.61 | sell fill 96.20 then 94.60 before 97.25: 0.61\n+ after touching 96.00, reach 94.30: 0.63 | short filled in the cluster returns to 95.00 before a high > 97.10: 0.69\ntouch 93.30: 0.61 | touch 93.40: 0.59 | break the 02 Nov low 93.83: 0.57 | base holds with no hourly close < 93.00: 0.57\n+ buy fill 93.40 then 94.80 before 92.80: 0.55 | 95.00 before 92.80: 0.49\n+ buy fill 93.25 then 95.20 before 92.20: 0.46 (joint 0.27 at P(fill) 0.59)\n+ a bounce to >= 95.00 occurs at some point: 0.75"];

  fresh [label="RE-ANCHOR 2026-11-02T10:05Z: live 94.41 (Binance last trade 09:57:22Z, bid/ask 94.40/94.41) vs 94.51 at capture = -0.11%.\nJev: structure unchanged and setup still valid 0.89 (auto); '0.11% decline materially changes the setup' 0.02 (auto);\n'another entry level would be materially better than 96.00' 0.25; 'waiting for a better price than 96.00 would materially improve the outcome' 0.19;\n'there is an unresolved decision-critical contradiction' 0.17. Re-anchored, no look-ahead used. 24h range still 93.18-95.95."];

  research [label="RESEARCH (Jev-set agenda: was the 29-30 Oct move fundamental or a market-wide flush? Jev rated the question decision-critical 0.55 and worth its cost 0.53 - i.e. unclear, so one query was run and its output was used as tie-breaking evidence, not as a forecast driver)\nFINDING: market-wide liquidation flush on the Binance hot-wallet compromise disclosed 2026-10-29T20:05Z ($6.3B, ~10 chains incl. Solana).\n $1.53B liquidated in 24h, 83.8% longs, SOL $82.6M; SOL -10.5% peak-to-trough vs BTC -6.5%, ETH -8.6%; common top and common break hour across the complex.\n Solana chain: no outage, no exploit (status page operational). Kamino paused SOL/BTC borrowing as a precaution, unaffected.\n Background supply: 1.02M SOL to seven venues over 5 days (Lookonchain, 29 Oct); spot ETF net outflows $27.69M (29 Oct) and $10.74M (30 Oct).\n Scheduled events inside 2026-11-02T10:00Z..2026-11-04T10:00Z: none with a market catalyst. Anza 'Create v4.5 branch' targeted 2 Nov has no delivery date; feature activation targeted 2026-11-09.\n Live catalyst in-window: Binance targeted a full Proof of Reserves report for Monday 2 Nov (today) - could move the whole complex either way, so it argues for a level-based order, not a market entry.\n Jev on the findings: whale/ETF flow tilts 48h lower 0.71; a worsening hack pushes through 93.18 rather than up through 96.44 0.73; containment and returning risk appetite breaks 96.44 and invalidates the short 0.56.\n NOT FOUND: a single authoritative 24h liquidation total for the exact window ($1.11B-$1.67B range reported); hourly SOL liquidation split; whether the 1.02M SOL deposits were sold; Binance's announcement page read directly (JS-gated); a primary total-market-cap index."];

  candL [label="CANDIDATE L - LONG in the base (rejected on arithmetic once the stop is placed honestly)\nL1 BUY LIMIT 93.40 / TP 94.80 / SL 92.80: G +1.4989% L -0.6424% RR 2.33 pBE 0.300, Jev P(TP first | fill) 0.55, P(fill) 0.59 -> binary EV/order +0.316%\n   BUT the 0.64% stop sits inside the 92.34-93.18 sweep zone; Jev: that stop is swept before the target 0.60, and a stop at 92.20 is far enough to survive a retest of 93.18 only 0.84. Same failure mode as LOSS-1.01%_2026-10-23T1024Z_ASTERUSDT. Rejected on structure, not on EV.\nL2 BUY LIMIT 93.40 / TP 94.80 / SL 92.20 (honest stop): G +1.4989% L -1.2848% RR 1.17 pBE 0.4615, p_TP 0.48 -> headroom +0.0185, binary EV/order +0.030% (3-branch +0.236%). Effectively break-even.\nL3 BUY LIMIT 93.25 / TP 95.20 / SL 92.20: G +2.0912% L -1.1260% RR 1.86 pBE 0.3500, p_TP 0.46 -> headroom +0.110, binary EV/order +0.209% (3-branch +0.411%). Genuinely viable, just dominated by the short on fill probability (0.59 vs 0.68) and on Jev's head-to-head.\nJev head-to-head: 'a sell limit in 95.90-96.20 is the better-founded expression than a buy limit in 93.25-93.40' = 0.75."];

  candS [label="CANDIDATE S - SHORT into the supply shelf (selected)\nS3 SELL LIMIT 96.00 / TP 94.30 / SL 97.20 / 48h: G +1.77083% L -1.25000% RR 1.417 pBE 0.41379\n   P(fill) 0.68 | P(TP before SL | fill) 0.55 | P(SL touched at all | fill) 0.27 | remainder 0.18 at +0.36% expiry payoff\n   EV/fill binary +0.4115% ; EV/order binary +0.2798% ; EV/fill 3-branch +0.7013% ; EV/order 3-branch +0.4769% ; headroom over pBE +0.1362\n   sensitivity: p_TP 0.65 -> +0.485% ; 0.45 -> +0.074% ; 0.414 -> +0.000% ; 0.35 -> -0.131% (binary)\n   structure: entry = upper edge of the 17-tag shelf, 1.67% above spot so it must be retested; TP 94.30 inside the box, 1.1% above the floor; stop 0.11 above the 97.09 measured extreme\nREJECTED ALTERNATIVES\nS1 sell 96.00 / TP 95.00 / SL 97.20: pBE 0.5455 vs p_TP 0.65, EV/order +0.163% - shallower target, less headroom than S3\nS2 sell 95.90 / TP 94.30 / SL 97.20: EV/order +0.318% (p_TP 0.61 at 95.90 vs 0.55 at 96.00 is a 0.1% level difference producing a 0.06 probability swing = measuring noise, so the conservative 0.55 reading was carried forward)\nS4 sell 96.20 / TP 94.60 / SL 97.25: EV/fill best of all (+0.589%) but P(fill) collapses to 0.46 (above the densest part of the cluster) -> EV/order +0.271%, no better than S3 with more fill risk\nMARKET entries rejected: a market short at 94.41 needs TP 93.20 before SL 95.10 = 0.53 against a break-even of about 0.53, i.e. zero edge; a market long at 94.41 needs TP 95.90 before SL 93.10 = 0.49. No structural anchor mid-box."];

  conflict [label="UNRESOLVED / CONTRADICTORY EVIDENCE (recorded, not smoothed over)\n1) The stop: '97.20 sits outside the routine overshoot envelope so an ordinary spike is unlikely to stop it' = 0.41, while the direct measurement 'touches 97.20 before expiry | fill' = 0.27. The 0.41 is defensible - 30 Oct printed 98.59 only 81h ago, so the 54h envelope really does reach 98.59. Resolved in favour of the direct conditional (0.27) and disclosed: this is the single largest downside risk, and p_TP would have to be wrong by 0.14 to erase the binary edge.\n2) Jev priced a 95.90 entry (0.61) better than a 96.00 entry (0.55) for the same target and stop, although the higher entry is strictly at least as good. Treated as noise; the lower number was used.\n3) 'Exhaustion, not a new leg' 0.51 against 'descending highs = sellers in control' 0.71. Both kept; the box read (0.69) is what the trade relies on, not either directional claim.\n4) Research resolved the cause of the flush but not its consequence: a liquidation wick normally mean-reverts (supports the base), while an unresolved $6.3B exchange compromise is a live trust shock with a PoR report due today (supports the break). The trade is long the second half of the box and does not depend on which wins."];

  forecast [label="INDEPENDENT FORECAST (contested; drawn in chart_prediction.svg and not adjusted to suit the order)\nup-probe first (ordering 0.55): 94.41 -> 96.05 at 2026-11-02T21:00Z (respects P(touch 96.00) 0.68 and P(>96.50 at expiry) 0.13, so the probe stops just above the shelf) -> rejection -> 94.30 by 03 Nov 08:00Z -> base test 93.30 at 03 Nov 18:00Z (respects P(touch 93.30) 0.61, P(close < 93.18) 0.38 and P(new low < 92.34) 0.24, so the base holds) -> drift back to 94.70 at 2026-11-04T10:00Z (inside the modal 94.00-96.00 endpoint band, 0.52).\nCONTESTED because the ordering is 0.55/0.45, the box-vs-break split is 0.69/0.25/0.38 with overlap, and the second half of the window is a coin flip between the base holding and the shelf being reclaimed.\nThe modal path happens to traverse the order's entry and target; that is a consequence of both levels being individually likely, not a reason to believe the order fills."];

  exec [label="EXECUTION: LIMIT is the only honest expression. The entry is a retest 1.67% above spot, so a MARKET entry cannot represent it, and breakout entries are out of scope for this journal.\nFill semantics: a sell limit fills when an hourly high touches 96.00; in the fill candle only the SL can trigger, so a 95.00-type target could not be credited in the same hour. Stated risk: a spike candle through 96.00 that also exceeds 97.20 stops the order in its own fill candle.\nP(no fill) = 0.32 and costs nothing in this model; an unfilled order is not a winning trade and is not counted as one."];

  go [label="GO: SHORT LIMIT 96.00, TP 94.30, SL 97.20, place 2026-11-02T10:10Z, expire 2026-11-04T10:00Z\nBoth sides were evaluated independently and both had positive expected value; the short was chosen on higher fill probability (0.68 vs 0.59), higher binary EV per order (+0.280% vs +0.209%), a stop outside the measured 97.09 extreme rather than inside the 92.34-93.18 sweep zone, and Jev's head-to-head at 0.75. NOT chosen on a directional preference.\nNo fees, funding or slippage exist in this journal model - a stated limitation, not a zero-cost assumption.", shape=box, style=bold];

  history -> chart; clock -> chart; chart -> scen -> lev -> fresh -> research -> candS;
  lev -> candL; research -> candL;
  candL -> conflict; candS -> conflict; conflict -> forecast -> exec -> go;
}